The project compiles. Here's the diagnosis and the patch.

## Root cause

With the reported settings (`enable-favorites-bar` = external bar ON, `history-hide` = Minimalistic UI ON, `favorites-hide` = "Hide favorites bar initially" ON), `ExperienceTweaks.isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()` is true, so the favorites bar is forced to `GONE` on every empty query (`updateSearchRecords`) and when the KISS bar closes (`onDisplayKissBar`).

The **only** code path that ever puts it back to `VISIBLE` is `doAction("display-history")`. But in the touch handlers of the `GestureDetector` that action was gated behind the unrelated *"Show history on touch"* preference (`history-onclick`):

```java
if (!prefs.getBoolean("double-tap", false)) {
    if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {   // <-- gate
        doAction("display-history");
    }
}
```

So if the user doesn't also enable "Show history on touch" (which the repro steps never do, and which is a *history* setting, not a favorites one), tapping the screen never runs the action and the favorites bar can never be revealed — exactly the reported behaviour ("no favorites bar, even after tapping the screen"). This also contradicts `qa-suite.md`, which states that with minimalistic mode for favorites, "Touching the screen on an empty area displays history and the favorites".

## Fix (`app/src/main/java/fr/neamar/kiss/forwarder/ExperienceTweaks.java`)

```diff
