             public boolean onSingleTapUp(MotionEvent e) {
-                // Double tap disabled: display history directly
+                // Double tap disabled: handle the tap directly
                 if(!prefs.getBoolean("double-tap", false)) {
-                    if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
-                        doAction("display-history");
-                    }
+                    onTap();
                 }
                 return super.onSingleTapUp(e);
             }

             @Override
             public boolean onSingleTapConfirmed(MotionEvent e) {
                 // Double tap enabled: wait to confirm this is indeed a single tap, not a double tap
                 if(prefs.getBoolean("double-tap", false)) {
-                    if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
-                        doAction("display-history");
-                    }
+                    onTap();
                 }
                 return super.onSingleTapConfirmed(e);
             }
+
+            /**
+             * Called when the user taps an empty area of the screen.
+             * Display the history if the user asked for it, and reveal the favorites bar when it
+             * is initially hidden: otherwise there would be no way at all to display favorites.
+             */
+            private void onTap() {
+                if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
+                    // Will also display the favorites bar when needed
+                    doAction("display-history");
+                } else {
+                    displayFavoritesBar();
+                }
+            }
@@ doAction(), case "display-history":
-                        if (isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()) {
-                            mainActivity.favoritesBar.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
-                        }
+                        displayFavoritesBar();
                         break;
@@ new helper
+    private void displayFavoritesBar() {
+        if (isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites() && mainActivity.isViewingSearchResults()) {
+            mainActivity.favoritesBar.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
+        }
+    }
```

Behaviour after the patch:

- Minimalistic UI + "Hide favorites bar initially": the bar is still hidden at startup, on search, and when the KISS bar closes, but **tapping an empty area of the screen now reveals it**, independently of "Show history on touch" (with that option on, history is still shown as well).
- The `display-history` gesture action (swipe up/down) behaves as before.
- The reveal is skipped while viewing all apps, where the external bar is intentionally hidden, so the existing favorites tests (`testExternalBarHiddenWhenViewingAllApps`, etc.) keep their semantics.
- Nothing changes when the hiding setting is off or the internal favorites bar is used.

`./gradlew clean assembleDebug` → **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**.

